---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const { grievanceOfficer } = site.legal;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Grievance redressal"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="How to raise a complaint with Virashu Private Limited, including the named grievance officer, the acknowledgement and resolution timelines, and how to escalate to the Data Protection Board or a consumer forum."
  lede="A named officer, a fixed timeline, and a route to escalate if we get it wrong."
  lastUpdated="19 September 2026"
>
  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    Every complaint that reaches us is logged and answered. We acknowledge receipt within{" "}
    <strong>{grievanceOfficer.acknowledgementWindow}</strong> and aim to resolve it within{" "}
    <strong>{grievanceOfficer.resolutionWindow}</strong> of receipt. If a matter needs longer, we tell
    you why and give you a date rather than leaving it open.
  </p>

  <h2>The grievance officer</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <td>{grievanceOfficer.name}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Designation</th>
        <td>{grievanceOfficer.designation}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Email</th>
        <td><span class="font-mono text-[0.875rem]">{grievanceOfficer.email}</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Postal address</th>
        <td>{site.legal.registeredOffice}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Acknowledgement</th>
        <td>Within {grievanceOfficer.acknowledgementWindow}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Resolution</th>
        <td>Within {grievanceOfficer.resolutionWindow}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    These timelines follow the requirements for intermediaries under the Information Technology
    (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, and the response
    expectations under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can raise</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy and personal data.</strong> Access, correction, erasure, withdrawal of consent,
      or a concern about how your data or photographs were handled.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hikkari platform conduct.</strong> A vendor who did not honour a quote, warranty or
      turnaround, or a vendor dispute about how the bidding treated them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Content on our services.</strong> Anything unlawful, misleading, or infringing your
      rights, including impersonation of you or your business.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Accessibility.</strong> Any part of our website or platform you cannot use, with the
      device and assistive technology you were using.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Any other matter</strong> concerning {site.legalName} or a group entity.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to file</h2>
  <p>
    Email the grievance officer with the subject line "Grievance" and include what happened, roughly
    when, which Hikkari request or account it concerns if applicable, and what outcome you are
    seeking. Attach any screenshots or documents that support it.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you would rather write in Hindi or another Indian language, do. We will respond in the language
    you used.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>We acknowledge the complaint and give you a reference number.</li>
    <li>We investigate, which may involve contacting the vendor or a group entity concerned.</li>
    <li>We tell you the outcome and the reason for it, in writing.</li>
    <li>
      If we cannot resolve it within {grievanceOfficer.resolutionWindow}, we tell you where it stands
      and when to expect the next update.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>If you are still not satisfied</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy matters.</strong> You may complain to the Data Protection Board of India under
      the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 after giving us the opportunity to resolve it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consumer matters.</strong> You may approach the appropriate Consumer Commission under
      the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, or the National Consumer Helpline.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cyber incidents.</strong> You may also report to the National Cyber Crime Reporting
      Portal where a criminal offence is involved.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    General enquiries that are not complaints should go through the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, where choosing the right desk gets you a faster reply.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
